WEBVTT

00:02:29.437 --> 00:02:30.438
believe it or not.

00:02:30.438 --> 00:02:31.522
(Laughing)

00:02:31.814 --> 00:02:33.566
I know you think
I invented twerking;

00:02:33.566 --> 00:02:34.567
I didn’t.

00:02:34.901 --> 00:02:37.111
I want you to know
where twerking came from.

00:02:37.486 --> 00:02:40.239
I think everyone should know
where everything comes from.

00:02:40.531 --> 00:02:42.992
You should know where
your food and water come from;

00:02:42.992 --> 00:02:45.161
you should know
where your clothes come from.

00:02:45.578 --> 00:02:48.915
It’s important to me to keep
the origin story of twerking alive.

00:02:49.373 --> 00:02:51.959
So here’s some farm-to-table for that ass.

00:02:51.959 --> 00:02:53.419
(Laughter)

00:02:53.419 --> 00:02:55.546
(Applause)

00:02:56.214 --> 00:02:59.425
Modern-day twerking derived
from Black people and Black culture.

00:02:59.675 --> 00:03:03.095
It has a direct parallel
to West African dances like mapouka.